  <h2>Dual Brain Robotics</h2>

  <p>
    Dual Brain Robotics occupies a unique position at the intersection of philosophy,
    cognitive science, artificial intelligence, and engineering.
  </p>

  <p>
    The project is not simply asking how to build smarter machines. It is exploring whether
    consciousness itself may require a fundamentally different architectural approach than
    today's dominant AI systems.
  </p>

  <p>
    The website is not saying, "We have built the robot." It is saying, "We have identified
    a potentially different way to think about the architecture of conscious systems."
  </p>

  <p>
    At Dual Brain Robotics, the distance between theory and application is both immense and
    surprisingly small. The engineering challenges are substantial, yet the conceptual
    blueprint already exists.
  </p>

  <p>
    Simply put: at Dual Brain Robotics, the journey from theory to application is always
    very near and very far away.
  </p>
